# Starlight docs conventions

## Content location

All documentation pages live in `docs/src/content/docs/`. Do not put doc content
elsewhere in the repo.

## File format

- Prefer `.md` for documentation pages.
- Use `.mdx` only when Starlight components are required (e.g. splash landing with `<Card>`).

## Sidebar sync

When adding, renaming, or removing a page, register the slug in
`docs/astro.config.mjs` so navigation links resolve. The site uses the
**`starlight-sidebar-topics`** plugin (not a flat `sidebar` array). Add new
pages under the appropriate topic's `items` tree — e.g. **Developer Docs →
Getting Started** for onboarding pages.

Current topics:

- **Developer Docs** (default) — Getting Started, Authoring, Tools, etc.
- **Architecture & RFCs** — subsystem RFCs and deep architecture
- **Agent Spec & LLMs** — AI agent reference

## Frontmatter

Every doc page needs at least `title` and `description` in YAML frontmatter.

## Package

The docs package is `@vam/docs`. Run commands from `docs/`:

```bash
pnpm dev
pnpm build
```
